{"name":"Moxie","hex":"#e5dad8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"moxie","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Nerve, spunk, strength of character.","Verve."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/moxie"}],"entries":[{"title":"Moxie","blocks":[{"text":"Moxie is a brand of carbonated beverage that is among the first mass-produced soft drinks in the United States. It was created around 1876 by Augustin Thompson as a patent medicine called \"Moxie Nerve Food\" and was produced in Lowell, Massachusetts. It is flavored with gentian root extract, an extremely bitter substance commonly used in herbal medicine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Moxie_soda%2C_full_logo.svg/330px-Moxie_soda%2C_full_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moxie","wikidata":"Q2078987"},{"title":"Moxie (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Moxie is a 2021 American comedy-drama film directed by Amy Poehler. Tamara Chestna and Dylan Meyer adapted the screenplay from the 2017 novel of the same name by Jennifer Mathieu. It stars Hadley Robinson, Alycia Pascual-Peña, Lauren Tsai, Patrick Schwarzenegger, Nico Hiraga, and Poehler."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f1/Moxie_film_poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moxie_(film)","wikidata":"Q73543906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/1914_-_Allentown_Independence_Day_Outing.jpg/500px-1914_-_Allentown_Independence_Day_Outing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/1914_-_Allentown_Independence_Day_Outing.jpg/1280px-1914_-_Allentown_Independence_Day_Outing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.or